Kubernetes Architecture
=>Control Plane (Master Components)

1.Apiserver
Entry point of Kubernetes cluster
All commands go through API server

2.etcd
Key-value database of Kubernetes
Stores cluster state and configuration
Stores:  Pods, Deployments, Secrets, ConfigMaps, Node information

3.kube-scheduler
Decides on which worker node a pod should run
Checks: CPU, Memory, Taints/tolerations, Affinity rules, Resource availability

4.kube-controller-manager
Runs controllers that continuously monitor cluster state.
Examples: Node Controller, ReplicaSet Controller, Deployment Controller

=>Worker Nodes
1.kubelet
Agent running on every worker node
Communicates with API server
Ensures containers are running properly

Responsibilities:
Starts pods
Monitors pod health
Runs liveness/readiness probes

2.kube-proxy
Handles networking inside cluster
Maintains iptables/ipvs rules
Enables pod-to-pod and service communication

Example:
When app pod accesses database service,
kube-proxy routes traffic correctly.


3.Container Runtime
Responsible for running containers.

